# Files that must NOT ship with the theme. One list, two consumers:
#   - scripts/deploy-theme.sh      (rsync --exclude-from, with --delete-excluded)
#   - scripts/release/package.sh   (rsync into a staging dir, then zip)
# rsync syntax; whole-line comments only (no inline "#"). A leading slash anchors
# to the theme root; an unanchored name matches at any depth.
#
# tools/*.json must ship. tools/ looks like a build-only directory, but
# inc/team-colors.php reads tools/contrast-rules.json at RUNTIME on every
# front-end team page (blueline_contrast_threshold()) to derive each team's
# readable foreground colour, and inc/settings/tokens.php reads
# tools/tokens.json. Excluding them would not fail loudly: the PHP falls back
# to hard-coded thresholds / an empty manifest and logs the fact (see
# blueline_contrast_rules_read_failure()), silently degrading every team page.
# Only the node scripts beside them (tools/*.mjs, tools/lib/) are dev tooling.
#
# assets/src/js/settings-{photos,brand-colors,occasions}.js must ship:
# inc/settings/admin-assets.php enqueues them straight from source. Every other
# assets/src/js file is bundled into one of the webpack entries
# (webpack.config.js), so it stays out (tests/DistIgnoreTest.php fails if an
# excluded file is not reachable from an entry). A new script enqueued from source needs
# its own "+" line here. rsync applies the first matching rule, so each "+"
# line must come before the "-" line it carves out of.
#
# assets/fonts/*.woff2 are the webpack inputs; the compiled CSS and the
# preload links use the copies in assets/dist/fonts/. The OFL licence texts
# in assets/fonts/ still ship.
#
# The assets/dist/*.js files listed below are the empty JavaScript stubs that
# @wordpress/scripts writes for CSS-only entries; nothing enqueues them
# (DistIgnoreTest checks they are still empty).
+ /assets/src/js/settings-photos.js
+ /assets/src/js/settings-brand-colors.js
+ /assets/src/js/settings-occasions.js
- /assets/src/js/*
/tools/*.mjs
/tools/lib
/assets/fonts/*.woff2
/assets/dist/editor.js
/assets/dist/sponsors-page.js
node_modules
vendor
